        <item>
            <title>1.0.27</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:05:08 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>205</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.27</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font: -apple-system-body, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  h3 { font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  ul { margin: 6px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
  p { margin: 6px 0; }
</style>
<h3>Improved</h3>
<ul>
<li>The menu bar panel now sits flat under the menu bar, like the Mac&#x27;s own Wi-Fi and Battery panels: no arrow, and the system&#x27;s see-through background in place of the solid one.</li>
<li>Press Esc to close the panel. It also closes when you switch desktop.</li>
<li>Opening the panel no longer takes you away from the app you are working in.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>After an Auto-Blast safety trip, fans on a curve or a Manual speed ease down to that speed and stay there. Before, they eased all the way down to their minimum and were handed back to macOS, so for about half a minute they could run far below your curve. Under a steady heavy load that let the Mac heat up again and trip Auto-Blast again, over and over.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
